<?xml-stylesheet type="text/xsl" href="ViewNLM-v2.3.xsl"?><!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD JATS (Z39.96) Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v1.0 20120330//EN" "JATS-archivearticle1.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" article-type="editorial"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">J Korean Med Sci</journal-id><journal-id journal-id-type="publisher-id">JKMS</journal-id><journal-title-group><journal-title>Journal of Korean Medical Science</journal-title></journal-title-group><issn pub-type="ppub">1011-8934</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1598-6357</issn><publisher><publisher-name>The Korean Academy of Medical Sciences</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2694383</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.3346/jkms.2007.22.S.S1</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Editor's Note</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>EDITOR'S NOTE - <italic>About This Supplement</italic></article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Cho</surname><given-names>Soo-Hun</given-names></name><role>Editor</role><xref ref-type="aff" rid="A1"/></contrib></contrib-group><aff id="A1">Journal of Korean Medical Science, Korea.</aff><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><month>9</month><year>2007</year></pub-date><pub-date pub-type="epub"><day>30</day><month>9</month><year>2007</year></pub-date><volume>22</volume><issue>Suppl</issue><fpage>S1</fpage><lpage>S1</lpage><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; 2007 The Korean Academy of Medical Sciences</copyright-statement><copyright-year>2007</copyright-year><license license-type="open-access" xlink:href="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/3.0"><license-p>This is an Open Access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution Non-Commercial License (<ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/3.0">http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/3.0</ext-link>) which permits unrestricted non-commercial use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.</license-p></license></permissions></article-meta></front><body><p>This supplemental issue of <italic>Journal of Korean Medical Science</italic> highlights cancer research in a variety of disciplines in Korea. For this special issue, the Editorial Board archived a series of recent contributions in cancer research in Korea, encompassing from reports on intriguing cases to animal studies, and from epidemiology to clinical trials.</p><p>Given the recent statistics showing that one out of every four Koreans is diagnosed with cancer during their lifetime, cancer is no doubt a major public health burden in Korea. In response to this, the Korean government has recently made a series of efforts to cope with this deadly disease, the most recent one of which is the legislation of the Cancer Control Act in 2003 and subsequent formulation and implementation of the National Cancer Control Programs (see page S3-4). Last year, the second-term cancer control plan for the following decade (2006-2015) was forged to strengthen the national cancer control activities, and the Editorial Board has decided that it is high time for the <italic>Journal</italic> to focus on cancer control and research activities in Korea.</p><p>I hope the readers of the <italic>Journal</italic> will have an in-depth look at the recent scientific efforts to fight against cancers in Korea. We also believe publishing this supplement will contribute to bring other accepted articles awaiting for their publication forward.</p></body></article>